      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. I'll write an improved version that:\n1. Uses a local variable for `Symmetry010Chronology.INSTANCE` to eliminate repetition\n2. Groups assertions logically with brief comments\n3. Extracts the opaque EPOCH_DAY arithmetic into named local variables\n4. Removes all the unused `data_*` methods (none are used by `test_Chronology_range`)Now let me compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored `test_Chronology_range` now uses a local `chrono` variable to avoid repeating `Symmetry010Chronology.INSTANCE`, groups assertions by logical category with explanatory comments, and extracts the opaque EPOCH_DAY arithmetic into named local variables (`maxYearDays`, `leapWeekDays`, `epochDayOffset`) that explain what each number represents."
